Z||000007||TwisT||01-30-2001||12:23 AM||||It would be nice to find the owner of this machine...  maybe he could give us some insight on what he did.  It's amazing how the Sunfire's lights have a profile that match the Fiero GT's nose-cone so well.  <P>I can imagine that this mod might not be too hard to perform,  providing you have some skill making some basic mounting brackets.  You could then either weld them on yourself,  or have a good shop to do it for you.  The cutting of the nose looks fairly straight-forward.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Black88GT||01-30-2001||12:31 AM||||If memory serves correct, last time this was brought up, theogre pointed out that the mod was illegal.<P>Also, the mirrors are hideously ugly, but he does get the originality award...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">             <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
