Z||000011||Oreif||01-30-2001||01:56 AM||||The only reason I could think of why it could be illegal would be height off the ground. I think headlights are required to be a certain distance above the ground. <BR>I personally don't like the look. (would like to see a pic with the hood closed) But I think it looks better than some of the other headlight mods I've seen. I like the spoiler in back but I think the side scoops look too homemade.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Philphine||01-30-2001||02:00 AM||||hey, thats the mustang wing i have. first time i've seen it on another fiero. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||TwisT||01-30-2001||02:11 AM||||Depending on your personal taste and preferences,  the headlights might be too much.  I agree the gaudyness of the side-scoop,  and the paint looks great until the flame jobby.  But I can also appreciate this guys creativity.  At least he's tried making a unique Fiero...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>The legality of these headlights is a good question...  though I'm not sure I'd be particularly worried around here (SD).  Cars have all sorts of mods these days...  and rarely do you see problems with the local authorities.  <P>Guess it amounts to having some balls...  lol<P>Brett<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||ur2biteme||01-30-2001||02:30 AM||||correct me if i'm wrong, but the reason i seem to recall for changing the headlights to anything other than what came stock being illegal, regardless of better visibility has to do with the way the DOT just plain doesnt want this stuff altered.  no good reason why (other than the foglights being used as headlights, and such) it should be this way.  i think it has a lot to do with bean counting, being that both lights involved (stock fiero and the sunfire lights) are both DOT approved.<P>This is what i think i've heard, i could be wrong.<P>------------------<BR>Bob's '87 econo coupe<BR>170k awaiting a tranny:(<BR> <A HREF="http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme" TARGET=_blank>http://members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||beer_stud_21||01-30-2001||04:25 AM||||I'm sorry, but those headlights are butt @#$% ugly...  So is the front of the sunfire for the same reason.  sunfire and ford focus have ugly front ends because of their headlights.  the mirriors are ugly too.  If it were me id put the stock mirriors back on, and undo the headlights, take the wing off and strip off the gaudy stickers.  Oh, and make sure there isn't a type-r sticker hiding anywhere.  hehe  I love the yellow color tho.  I have a thing for "tweety bird" yellow cars.  What i think might look good on a fiero is big sunk in running lights like are on mid 90s trans ams i believe...  I don't know my GM cars that well yet but I think you guys will know the ones i mean.  i think something like that would look really good on a fiero if someone could do some quality body work.  Sorry if I was a little harsh on this guys car.  To each his own i guess....<P>-Marlin||||reg||13
Z||000016||FieroLisa||01-30-2001||11:11 AM||||That car was parked right next to me at Carlisle (woo hoo see my gold bumper on its left) Anyway the headlights looked interesting until you got up close. Because of the shape of the headlights and the shape of the fascia, it just didn't quite fit right, the curves were off. It didn't look bad, but it just didn't look...right.<P>I give the guy a lot of credit for doing a good a job as he did on it though. It's not his fault those headlights were not supposed to fit on a Fiero.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
